_refine.details                                  
;WATER MOLECULE 345 IS SURROUNDED BY THREE POSITIVELY
CHANGED RESIDUES:  ARG 245, LYS 193, AND SYMMETRY-RELATED
LYS 290.  HOWEVER, THE DENSITY IS NOT GOOD ENOUGH TO
IDENTIFY WHAT IT MIGHT BE.

WATER MOLECULE 392 IS SITUATED IN BETWEEN TWO DNA PHOSPHATE
GROUPS OF A 430 D AND T 431 D.  CA-ACETATE WAS USED AS
BUFFER.  HOWEVER, THE DENSITY IS NOT GOOD ENOUGH TO
DETERMINE WHETHER IT IS A CA(2+) FOR SURE.
;
